          "Title": "curl: curl: TFTP direction confusion",
          "Description": "libcurl's TFTP state machine fails to validate state transitions against the\nrequested transfer direction, accepting opening server responses for both\nreads and writes interchangeably. A malicious TFTP server can respond to a\ndownload request in a way that forces the client into transmit mode, prompting\nlibcurl to consume and transmit data from the handle's persistent\n`CURLOPT_READDATA` pointer - including data remaining from unrelated prior\noperations, such as an HTTP POST request executed on a reused handle.",
          "Severity": "LOW",
